{
 "model": "Hofstede national culture dimensions (6-D data matrix; engine uses the classic 5-D subset PDI/IDV/MAS/UAI/LTO by default)",
 "dimensions": {
  "pdi": "Power Distance",
  "idv": "Individualism",
  "mas": "Masculinity",
  "uai": "Uncertainty Avoidance",
  "lto": "Long-Term Orientation (WVS-based, 2010)",
  "ivr": "Indulgence vs Restraint (2010)"
 },
 "note": "Values are Geert Hofstede's 'Dimension data matrix' (2015 release, geerthofstede.com), obtained from the plotly/datasets mirror because geerthofstede.com and hofstede-insights.com are egress-blocked in this environment; the column layout (ctr, pdi, idv, mas, uai, ltowvs, ivr) and known anchor values (Turkey 66/37/45/85/46/49, Great Britain 35/89/66/35/51/69, Spain 57/51/42/86/48/44, Slovakia PDI 104 / MAS 110, Greece UAI 112) match the published matrix. Regional entries (Arab countries, Africa West/East) are used as proxies ONLY for the countries Hofstede lists as members of those samples. Countries with no score (e.g. Senegal, Côte d'Ivoire, Cameroon, Azerbaijan on the core four) return no cultural-distance score rather than a guess. ENG/SCO/WAL/NIR are aliases of GBR (Hofstede scored the UK as one unit). Re-verify against geerthofstede.com before commercial use.",
